//? Title: Line RANSAC: actual sampled hypotheses, TLS refits and separately scored consensus
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Gross outliers can pull an all-point least-squares line away from a dominant
geometric relation. RANSAC scores line hypotheses from tiny random samples and
refits the best consensus. Actual native index draws and scored masks now expose
both skipped trials and real winning hypotheses. The original 80 noisy line
points,40 outliers and seeds7/1 remain; pre-refit and post-refit consensus are
reported separately.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

A noncoincident pair defines an implicit line normalized so that its residual is
a perpendicular distance. A trial consensus is
$$ I=\{k:|a x_k+b y_k+c|\le\tau\},\qquad a^2+b^2=1. $$
\alttext(The actual represented normalized-line residual selects points within a fixed distance threshold.)
The native producer retains the first strictly largest minimal-model consensus,
then orthogonally refits those points by their principal scatter direction.
Refitting changes coefficients, so it rescans the returned line and reports a
separate post-refit mask. Returning the old mask with new coefficients would
confuse two different decisions.

The familiar ideal independent-sample bound is ceil(log(1-p)/log(1-w^s)). This
implementation draws two independent indices and skips duplicates. With I known
inliers among N stored points, its exact distinct-inlier-pair probability is
I(I-1)/N^2 before geometric degeneracy. Coincident inlier coordinates or an
unsuitable threshold can lower valid-model probability further. No finite
positive-success bound exists for zero good-sample probability, and that case
now throws rather than returning one trial.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ransac_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/prufer.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/flow_diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/hull_algorithms.hpp>
#include <datamunge/random/sampling_analysis.hpp>
#include <iomanip>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/qr_algorithm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/lm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/arithmetic_coding.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/rbf.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/model_plot.hpp>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/ransac.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t =
        a::ransac_line_trace({0, 1, 2, 3, 2}, {1, 3, 5, 7, -4}, .05, 20, 1);
    const auto it =
        std::find_if(t.trials.begin(), t.trials.end(), [](const auto &s) {
        return s.kind == a::RansacTrialKind::Scored;
    });
    const auto &s = *it;
    std::print("\n| actual attempt (first8) | first id | second id | kind (duplicate0,coincident1,scored2) " "| consensus | improved |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < std::min<std::size_t>(8, t.trials.size()); ++i) {
        const auto &e = t.trials[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", e.iteration, e.first,
                   e.second, int(e.kind), e.count, e.improved);
    }

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first scored index pair\n{} / {}", s.first,
                       s.second));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual first scored consensus\n{}", s.count));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual winning / refitted counts\n{} / {}",
                       t.hypothesis.inlier_count, t.line.inlier_count));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/ransac_tiny.svg");
}
```
